 * one of `value`/`values` is populated per row (scalar rows use `value`,
 * list-shaped rows use `values`); both are their zero value when the other
 * is set. Row ORDER within OdinTemplateDetail.infobox is load-bearing —
 * upstream authors group related facts positionally (see
 * extract_infobox_facts' population-extraction rule, which walks forward
 * from a parent row) — and values are passed through exactly as cached,
 * with no scrubbing of incoherent or self-referential upstream data.
